;;; **An unsat core that holds a nested fact** (P1e2.3's S8).
;;;
;;; Written for M1e2's survey (2026-10-14) as `probes/nested-core.ein`: the
;;; unsat core contains a given negative fact, `(not (p A))`, whose argument is
;;; a fact. The walk's read-out printed it as a struct repr,
;;; `(not Fact(relation_name='p', args=('A',)))`. Gone since M1e2 S1e2.1a.5's
;;; switch: the region read-out prints a core as s-expressions,
;;;
;;;   unsat core        (not (p A))
;;;   unsat core        (q A)
;;;   refuted by        boom
;;;
;;; Banked here by M1e2 S1e2.3.4 (the user's ruling (a) of 2026-11-03, *pin
;;; both*): it is the only program known to print a nested fact in a core, and
;;; nothing checked the spelling. `ein-cli/tests/read_out.rs` asserts the
;;; line, and `corpus_shapes.md5`'s read-out digests hold the block.

(relation p T :why "p holds of {?1}")
(relation q T :why "q holds of {?1}")
(not (p A))
(q A)
(rule boom () :match (and (not (p ?x)) (q ?x)) :assert (false) :why "p is false of {?x} and q holds of {?x}, which cannot both be")
